* History
Functional programming is old, but some major languages have adapted them quite recently

- LISP in 1958. Introduced functional paradigm in its programming language
- JavaScript 1995 (original idea was to embed Scheme into HTML, a functional language)
- C# 3.0 in 2007
- Go 2009
- C++ 11 in 2011
- Java 8 in 2014
- Rust 2015

: LISP: John McCarthy, 1958 am MIT.
: C# 3.0 erschien im November 2007 mit Lambda-Ausdrücken (für LINQ). C# 2.0 (2005) hatte bereits anonyme Methoden.
: Go hatte Funktionsliterale und Closures von Anfang an.

