* How to make random() pure? The answer

- *Pseudo* *random:* Pass the state (seed) in and return the new state

#lang go

    func next(seed uint32) (value uint32, newSeed uint32) {
        newSeed = seed*1664525 + 1013904223
        return newSeed >> 16, newSeed
    }

    v1, s := next(42) // next(42) always returns the same value
    v2, _ := next(s)

- *Real* *random:* Pass the "state of the world" in and return a new world
- Haskell does this with the IO type ← Next lecture

: "An interactive program is a pure function that takes the current 'state of the world' as its arg and produces a modified world as result" - unknown Twitter user

