* Evaluate these expressions. The answer

    (λx.x) a          = a
    (λx.a) b          = a
    (λx.λy.y) a b     = (λy.y) b = b
    (λx.λy.x) a b     = (λy.a) b = a

- `λx.λy.x` takes two arguments and returns the first one
- `λx.λy.y` takes two arguments and returns the second one
- We call them TRUE and FALSE

* Your turn: Boolean logic with functions

    TRUE  := λa.λb.a
    FALSE := λa.λb.b
    NOT   := λp.(p FALSE TRUE)

