* Lambda Calculus in JavaScript
#lang javascript

  TRUE = a => b => a;
  FALSE = a => b => b;
  NOT = f => a => b => f(b)(a);

  ToBool = f => f(() => true)(() => false)()

  console.log( ToBool(TRUE) ) // -> true
  console.log( ToBool(FALSE) ) // -> false

  console.log( ToBool(NOT(TRUE)) )  // -> false
  console.log( ToBool(NOT(FALSE)) ) // -> true

.link https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3VQ382QG-y4 Fundamentals of Lambda Calculus & Functional Programming in JavaScript

* Lambda Calculus: Why did we do this?

- With functions alone, we built TRUE, FALSE, NOT, AND and OR
- With functions alone, you can also build numbers, recursion and every computation (Church-Turing thesis)
- Every lambda in Go, Java or JavaScript is a λ from 1936
- Haskell is, at its core, lambda calculus with types ← Next lecture

: Lambda-Kalkül und Turingmaschine können genau dasselbe berechnen. Die Turingmaschine ist das Modell für imperative Sprachen (Zustand, Speicher), der Lambda-Kalkül für funktionale (nur Funktionen).

